From 153b5ce1db45cce9763ab2daf28b57edb2404193 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emagip_ <72194496+Emagip@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:23:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: omap_hsmmc: restore single-block quirk for OMAP34xx
 ES2.1 with DM_MMC

OMAP34xx/35xx silicon revisions 2.1 and older cannot do multiple block
reads on MMC1/MMC2 in polling or interrupt mode (SPRZ278F, advisory
2.1.1.128): data is corrupted once the controller's two 512-byte read
buffers are full. The legacy omap_hsmmc_init() path limits b_max to 1 on
these revisions, but the driver-model path (omap_hsmmc_of_to_plat) lost
that check, so SPL fails on such boards with:

  Error reading cluster
  spl_load_image_fat: error reading image u-boot.img, err - -5

Apply the same limit in the DM path. Found on a TMDSEVM3530
(OMAP3530 ES2.1, main board Rev D).

Signed-off-by: Emagip_ <72194496+Emagip@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/mmc/omap_hsmmc.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/omap_hsmmc.c b/drivers/mmc/omap_hsmmc.c
index 2cf3e4e5..3751c475 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/omap_hsmmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/omap_hsmmc.c
@@ -1928,6 +1928,14 @@ static int omap_hsmmc_of_to_plat(struct udevice *dev)
 	cfg->f_min = 400000;
 	cfg->voltages = MMC_VDD_32_33 | MMC_VDD_33_34 | MMC_VDD_165_195;
 	cfg->b_max = CONFIG_SYS_MMC_MAX_BLK_COUNT;
+#if defined(CONFIG_OMAP34XX)
+	/*
+	 * Silicon revs 2.1 and older do not support multiblock transfers
+	 * (OMAP35x errata SPRZ278F, advisory 2.1.1.128).
+	 */
+	if ((get_cpu_family() == CPU_OMAP34XX) && (get_cpu_rev() <= CPU_3XX_ES21))
+		cfg->b_max = 1;
+#endif
 	if (fdtdec_get_bool(fdt, node, "ti,dual-volt"))
 		plat->controller_flags |= OMAP_HSMMC_SUPPORTS_DUAL_VOLT;
 	if (fdtdec_get_bool(fdt, node, "no-1-8-v"))
-- 
2.53.0

